{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000ca89","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0c6d9-138d-7c82-92f1-7d0657d57a0f"},"sequence":927,"recorded_at":1780531400001849,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"69dcebcf-aab8-4829-be62-f7110c555cc6","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"69dcebcf-aab8-4829-be62-f7110c555cc6","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"69dcebcf-aab8-4829-be62-f7110c555cc6"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0c6dd-fc8f-7b12-9d64-6222fa09b708"},"task_id":"01a0c6dd-fc8f-7b12-9d64-6222fa09b708","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0c6dd-fc8f-7b12-9d64-6222fa09b708","chunk":"Read text file `internal/secprim/open_member_unix.go`.\n1|//go:build !windows\n2|\n3|package secprim\n4|\n5|import (\n6|\t\"errors\"\n7|\t\"os\"\n8|\n9|\t\"golang.org/x/sys/unix\"\n10|)\n11|\n12|// openCommitRelative walks one validated member from the staging-root\n13|// directory handle to an open file descriptor without ever re-resolving\n14|// a path string: every component is opened relative to the previous\n15|// component's descriptor with openat. Intermediate components carry\n16|// O_NOFOLLOW|O_DIRECTORY, so a symlinked directory on the path fails\n17|// with ELOOP instead of redirecting the walk outside the root; the\n18|// final component carries O_NOFOLLOW|O_NONBLOCK, so a trailing symlink\n19|// fails with ELOOP and a FIFO returns immediately instead of stalling\n20|// the opener until a writer appears. Descriptors pin what they opened:\n21|// a rename or swap after any step cannot retarget a descriptor the\n22|// walk already holds, which is what closes the validate-then-open\n23|// TOCTOU rather than repeating it with more steps.\n24|//\n25|// The walk reports no refusal of its own: ELOOP maps to the shared\n26|// errCommitSymlink signal (refused as \"member symlink escape\" by the\n27|// caller) and every other failure returns raw (refused as \"open\n28|// failed\" with its cause). Shape checks on the final descriptor stay\n29|// with the caller, which stats the descriptor rather than the path.\n30|//\n31|// rootPath is the guard root the caller already bound to root with\n32|// guardRootMatches before descending: the walk descends from the\n33|// handle alone because descriptors pin what they opened, while the\n34|// Windows walk descends from the verified path string. Both name the\n35|// same directory past the shared binding check, so the containment\n36|// root is one value on both platforms, not one per walk.\n37|//\n38|// Error classification runs before any descriptor is closed: from the\n39|// second intermediate onward previous == current, so closing first\n40|// would fstat a recycled descriptor number and misreport the shape.\n41|func openCommitRelative(root *os.File, rootPath string, member string, segments []string) (*os.File, error) {\n42|\t// rootPath names the guard root already bound to root by the\n43|\t// caller; it is documentation here, enforcement in Guard.Open.\n44|\t_ = rootPath\n45|\tprevious := -1\n46|\tcurrent := int(root.Fd())\n47|\tfor _, segment := range segments[:len(segments)-1] {\n48|\t\tnext, err := unix.Openat(current, segment,\n49|\t\t\tunix.O_RDONLY|unix.O_NOFOLLOW|unix.O_DIRECTORY|unix.O_CLOEXEC, 0)\n50|\t\tif err != nil {\n51|\t\t\tclassified := classifyCommitErr(current, segment, err)\n52|\t\t\tif previous >= 0 {\n53|\t\t\t\t_ = unix.Close(previous)\n54|\t\t\t}\n55|\t\t\treturn nil, classified\n56|\t\t}\n57|\t\tif previous >= 0 {\n58|\t\t\t_ = unix.Close(previous)\n59|\t\t}\n60|\t\tprevious, current = next, next\n61|\t}\n62|\tlast := segments[len(segments)-1]\n63|\tfinal, err := unix.Openat(current, last,\n64|\t\tunix.O_RDONLY|unix.O_NOFOLLOW|unix.O_CLOEXEC|unix.O_NONBLOCK, 0)\n65|\tif err != nil {\n66|\t\tclassified := classifyCommitErr(current, last, err)\n67|\t\tif previous >= 0 {\n68|\t\t\t_ = unix.Close(previous)\n69|\t\t}\n70|\t\treturn nil, classified\n71|\t}\n72|\tif previous >= 0 {\n73|\t\t_ = unix.Close(previous)\n74|\t}\n75|\treturn os.NewFile(uintptr(final), member), nil\n76|}\n77|\n78|// classifyCommitErr sorts the walk failures: a symlink anywhere on the\n79|// path becomes the escape signal, while a missing component, a file\n80|// where a directory stands, or a permission failure stays raw for the\n81|// caller's open-failed refusal.\n82|//\n83|// The errno alone does not name the shape on every kernel: Linux\n84|// reports ELOOP for an O_NOFOLLOW openat meeting a symlink, while\n85|// Darwin reports ENOTDIR for the O_DIRECTORY half of the same event.\n86|// Either errno therefore re-examines the component with fstatat at\n87|// AT_SYMLINK_NOFOLLOW — still relative to the parent descriptor, so\n88|// no path string is re-resolved — and only a component that is a\n89|// symlink right now becomes the escape signal. A swap between the\n90|// failed open and this check fails closed in every direction: each\n91|// outcome (symlink, directory, missing) refuses, and only the rule\n92|// name differs.\n93|func classifyCommitErr(parent int, segment string, err error) error {\n94|\tif errors.Is(err, unix.ELOOP) {\n95|\t\treturn errCommitSymlink\n96|\t}\n97|\tif errors.Is(err, unix.ENOTDIR) {\n98|\t\tvar status unix.Stat_t\n99|\t\tif fstatErr := unix.Fstatat(parent, segment, &status, unix.AT_SYMLINK_NOFOLLOW); fstatErr == nil {\n100|\t\t\tif status.Mode&unix.S_IFMT == unix.S_IFLNK {\n101|\t\t\t\treturn errCommitSymlink\n102|\t\t\t}\n103|\t\t}\n104|\t}\n105|\treturn err\n106|}\n107|\n108|// clearNonblock drops O_NONBLOCK from an admitted regular file so a\n109|// borrowed descriptor never leaks the flag to its reader. Regular-file\n110|// reads ignore the flag either way.\n111|func clearNonblock(file *os.File) error {\n112|\treturn unix.SetNonblock(int(file.Fd()), false)\n113|}","final_result":true}}}
