{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000cff9","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0c6d9-138d-7c82-92f1-7d0657d57a0f"},"sequence":1623,"recorded_at":1780531400003241,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"69dcebcf-aab8-4829-be62-f7110c555cc6","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"69dcebcf-aab8-4829-be62-f7110c555cc6","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"69dcebcf-aab8-4829-be62-f7110c555cc6"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0c6ed-685a-7e11-af2b-90ddc3fea697"},"task_id":"01a0c6ed-685a-7e11-af2b-90ddc3fea697","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0c6ed-685a-7e11-af2b-90ddc3fea697","chunk":"edited\nchanged lines: lines 16-24\n--- original\n+++ updated\n@@\n-// RunResult is one completed process execution: the exit code is data,\n-// never an error. A nonzero exit from a well-formed probe (has-session\n-// against a missing session reports exit 1) proves the negative; only a\n-// transport failure — the process never ran — returns an error, and an\n-// error proves nothing, not even non-commit.\n-type RunResult struct {\n-\tStdout   []byte\n-\tExitCode int\n-}\n+// RunResult is one completed process execution: the exit code and both\n+// streams are data, never an error. A nonzero exit alone proves\n+// nothing: tmux reports every failure with exit 1 (verified on 3.6a),\n+// so absence is proven only by an exit paired with its absence-shaped\n+// stderr (see classifyAbsence); only a transport failure — the process\n+// never ran, or died by signal — returns an error, and an error proves\n+// nothing, not even non-commit.\n+type RunResult struct {\n+\tStdout   []byte\n+\tStderr   []byte\n+\tExitCode int\n+}\n","final_result":true}}}
