he zero report); replay\n482|session/corrupt (+6 pinned members); fencingmap force/invalid (+3\n483|pinned members); dialstale refused/missing; probedeps\n484|dialer/admission; bind wiring placement/verify; sunpath helper/EXE\n485|8-op/prober; placement gate/prober; leafwiring 2 sites; presentmemory\n486|helper/dispatch/observer; triple helper/dispatch; boundarywait\n487|helper/dispatch; waitlesser/stoplesser min/fallback; bindmap\n488|coded/uncoded; evidence digest/forged.\n489|\n490|Ratio: 168 measured of 3648 (50+10+108 M across Tables A/B/D;\n491|Table C all U); 34 bound; 3446 unreachable with reasons. Every\n492|driven refusal direction is measured except the bound cells: 22\n493|driven but rowless (B22 singletons/forks, B23 normalized details,\n494|B29 poll past-deadline, B30 mappings, B32 propagation) and 8 named\n495|undriven gaps (B24/B25/B26/B28/B31 cells, B29 dispatch side), each\n496|with its owner below.\n497|\n498|## Stated bounds\n499|\n500|- B1 Determinism: no row has a real-tmux witness. Every broker, server,\n501|  and spawner interaction runs through injected dependencies; the suite\n502|  passes with no tmux process anywhere. A live-server test would add a\n503|  witness, not a rule, and is sibling scope.\n504|- B2 Windows refusal: native Windows MUST NOT claim tmux (pinned SPEC\n505|  1458). The Windows platform refuses at the lexical gate on every host\n506|  (row 15); the Windows commit/verify arms refuse every platform and\n507|  exist only so the package compiles under GOOS=windows.\n508|- B3 Nil-dependency weakening on the foreground path panics instead of\n509|  misbehaving; the narrowing row pins the refusal and discloses the\n510|  panic kill.\n511|- B4 No gate inspects source text, so no token-preserving mutant\n512|  applies; the harness executes the behavioral suite.\n513|- B5 Attach presentation vectors are sibling scope: attached and broker\n514|  outcomes carry the socket, and only the spawned outcome carries argv.\n515|- B6 Lifecycle operations (create, attach, status, quiesce, stop,\n516|  terminate, restore) belong to the sibling leaves, not to acquisition.\n517|- B7 The handle-mismatch arm stages its race through the sameDirectory\n518|  seam; a true concurrent handle swap is not staged.\n519|- B8 Registry bindings and the digest re-pin belong to the story's\n520|  final leaf; this leaf documents clause coverage here and in the\n521|  conformance matrix only.\n522|- B9 Adapter split: this leaf ships the decision core and argv only. No\n523|  production probe or spawner implementation exists in the tree; the\n524|  exec/probe adapters that report Reconcile/ResolveEvidence verdicts\n525|  and spawn through the built argv, and the server socket's crash\n526|  evidence, are owned by the lifecycle leaf TASK-260830-1c28dz. The\n527|  no-fallback proof covers spawns routed through Dependencies.Spawn;\n528|  a fallback through a direct os/exec call is excluded today only by\n529|  the import census (no os/exec import in the package).\n530|  Dependencies.Spawn is inert on the background path: a nil spawner\n531|  with a live broker still contacts (the broker path never calls it),\n532|  so the field is dead weight there — which is what makes the\n533|  shared-Dependencies fallback shape realistic, and why the spy\n534|  census arms the foreground probe alongside the spawner.\n535|- B10 Crash convergence assumes a umask that preserves owner rwx\n536|  (umask & 0700 == 0). Under an owner-bit-stripping umask a leaf\n537|  stranded between mkdirat and the explicit chmod refuses on retry\n538|  instead of converging, because existing leaves verify, never repair.\n539|- B11 A symlinked intermediate component inside the root path is\n540|  followed; only the root's last component refuses (row 9). This\n541|  matches the landed secprim root open and is the same bound.\n542|- B12 The landed argv shape refusal (BuildArgv via secprim.CheckArgv)\n543|  is reachable only by direct call with a non-filesystem runtime dir\n544|  (witnessed by TestBuildArgvRefusesInvalidArgvShape); through Acquire\n545|  the directory always names a created directory.\n546|- B13 Sentinel/smoke sufficiency, signature verification, liveness,\n547|  and expiry are the landed Reconcile admission's verdict, consumed\n548|  here through Has. This leaf decides membership plus generation\n549|  binding only; the host-binding and provider-build cross-bind the\n550|  wrapper evaluates stays with the lifecycle owner.\n551|- B14 The battery and the read-only-root test assume a non-root test\n552|  user: N-fchmod-umask admits non-root creates past the explicit\n553|  chmod, so under root it is equivalent to the original and survives,\n554|  and TestEnsureRuntimeDirRefusesReadOnlyRoot stages a genuine EACCES\n555|  only when permission bits bind the test user. The reviewer's\n556|  same-shaped plant carries the identical assumption.\n557|- B15 Unmeasured fail-closed stat arms, no seam: handleBoundToPath's\n558|  two stat-failure arms (runtime.go) and verifyOwnership's !ok arm\n559|  (ownership_unix.go) fail closed by code and are prose only by test —\n560|  no test can stage a Stat failure on an open directory handle, or a\n561|  stat without ownership metadata on unix, without a seam. The\n562|  guard.Resolve refusal arm (runtime.go) is unreachable through the\n563|  name grammar: every input the guard would refuse is refused earlier\n564|  by scalar, so the fail-open plant survives by construction. The\n565|  secprim.NewGuard refusal arm (runtime.go:94-96) is the same class:\n566|  no committed input reaches it. The same unstageable class covers\n567|  the commit-side Fchmod and parent-Fsync failure arms and the\n568|  commit-side (runtime_unix.go:76-79) and verify-side leaf-Stat\n569|  failure arms: no committed test stages those failures. An\n570|  unopenable (0000) root reports `runtime containment` on both entries\n571|  with no committed test staging it — classifying EACCES as missing\n572|  would reroute it to `runtime root`, refusal-to-refusal. Reported\n573|  as error-arm rows, never counted among the narrowing survivors.\n574|- B16 The collision gate compares cleaned byte strings: an ambient\n575|  value naming the derived socket through a symlinked or relative\n576|  alias of the root walks past it (realpath equivalence is not\n577|  applied, and a cwd-relative spelling never equals the absolute\n578|  derived socket). Roots containing a comma are outside the TMUX\n579|  member's encoding: the gate splits at the first comma exactly as\n580|  tmux(1) itself does, so a comma-root socket component walks past\n581|  it. The spec rule is unaffected — the socket is derived, never\n582|  selected from an ambient value — so this bounds only the\n583|  package-local defense-in-depth claim. An `ax` invocation from\n584|  inside its own AX pane refuses `ambient collision` when the caller\n585|  populates Ambient from the process environment\n586|  (TMUX=`<derived>`,pid,idx in the real encoding): over-strict\n587|  rather than over-permissive, and the caller owns what it observes\n588|  — the lifecycle leaf TASK-260830-1c28dz decides the\n589|  nested-invocation rule deliberately.\n590|- B17 The mode gate reads permission bits only: setgid/sticky bits on\n591|  a 0700 leaf are admitted and macOS ACLs are not inspected. This\n592|  matches the landed hosttrust custody precedent\n593|  (internal/hosttrust/custody_unix.go platformModeOK: Perm() == mode),\n594|  so it is the same bound, not a fork.\n595|- B18 The derived socket path is not checked against the platform\n596|  sun_path limit (104 bytes on macOS); a deep runtime root surfaces\n597|  as a spawn failure in the lifecycle leaf's adapter, owned by\n598|  TASK-260830-1c28dz.\n599|- B19 The Runtime IPC root's own mode and ownership are not gated in\n600|  this leaf: the root arrives as the caller-supplied\n601|  localstore-resolved PathRuntime value, its creation-time custody is\n602|  the localstore layout owner's, and the SPEC 810-812\n603|  before-bind/connect rejection of an unsafe path, parent, or ancestor\n604|  is the lifecycle bind step's (TASK-260830-1c28dz), which is the step\n605|  that binds. This leaf pins the root handle (no-follow open plus\n606|  handle/path binding) and commits the leaf relative to it; a\n607|  world-writable root is admitted here and refused at bind. That the\n608|  root value is the landed localstore PathRuntime is a contract\n609|  statement about the caller, not a driven fact: no test composes\n610|  localstore with Acquire.\n611|- B20 Whether the runtime leaf was created by AX is indistinguishable\n612|  after the fact: any same-user 0700 directory under an admitted name\n613|  is accepted. The verifiable properties — mode, ownership, kind,\n614|  containment — are gated (rows 1-15); provenance is not claimed.\n615|- B21 No broker is modelled as the zero BrokerReport, whose\n616|  Principal.UID is 0: for a non-root process the absent broker\n617|  refuses on the authentication arm, while under a root process the\n618|  same-user arm passes and refusal comes from the generation arm.\n619|  The broker-path outcome socket binding is the generation equality\n620|  only — BrokerReport carries no socket of its own.\n621|- B22 Singleton arms ship no narrowing mutant: admitting the\n622|  singleton refused member is deleting the gate. Covered sites, each\n623|  test-pinned in both directions where a fork exists: create relay\n624|  transport (relay), descriptor presence fork (descpresence),\n625|  attach admission nil (serveadmitnil), spawner runner nil\n626|  (spawnnil), reconcile verifier nil (reconcilenil), states root\n627|  empty (stateopen), persist/attach stores nil (storenil),\n628|  failed-kill self-confirm (selfconfirm), live-after-escalation\n629|  (stoptimeout). Owner: this leaf; retest if any site grows a\n630|  second refused member.\n631|- B23 The landed status engine normalizes backend error details to\n632|  \"status observation unknown\" (coded or not), so the cutrow and\n633|  empty-panes narrowings measure at the helper entries while the\n634|  dispatch legs pin the code. Owner: this leaf; retest if the\n635|  engine stops normalizing.\n636|- B24 The idempotency-store Completed read-failure arm is unstaged:\n637|  no seam fails receipt reads (hooks fire on write paths only).\n638|  Owner: hardening; stage with a read-failure seam to measure.\n639|- B25 The Bind clean-miss sub-arm is unstageable: every Bind error\n640|  the hooks stage leaves the committed file, so Lookup always finds\n641|  it. The clean-found sub-arm is measured (N-bind-hook-found).\n642|  Owner: hardening.\n643|- B26 The attach effect-failure dispatch mapping is unstaged: no\n644|  committed failure reaches it (the store replays identical\n645|  receipts; conflicting receipts are untested at dispatch).\n646|  Owner: hardening.\n647|- B27 No committed test composes the Production Dependencies into\n648|  Acquire: AFG reaches the adapter and bind gates only through\n649|  caller-injected implementations (the 19 Table C U2c cells). The\n650|  injection seam is first-leaf-owned; Production wiring is\n651|  unit-pinned (TestProductionWiresDependencies). Owner: composition\n652|  test, sibling scope.\n653|- B28 The backend command-error wrap is unmeasured at PFX (no\n654|  backend test stages a refused build; the builder rows pin the\n655|  refused shapes at CMD). Owner: this leaf; retest with a\n656|  refused-build backend test.\n657|- B29 The close-confirm poll deadline is pinned for past-deadline\n658|  at PFX via direct staging; the exact-boundary member and\n659|  dispatch-level staging are unmeasured (the fake runner advances\n660|  no time). Owner: hardening.\n661|- B30 The OSRunner exit/transport/argv mappings are total functions\n662|  over uncoded inputs with no refused class to admit a member of;\n663|  four tests pin them including a real-exec scrub integration.\n664|  Owner: this leaf.\n665|- B31 The custody root-ownership arm is untested and singleton: the\n666|  ownership seam stages leaf-first (the leaf refuses before the\n667|  root arm runs), and a truly foreign root needs privilege. Owner:\n668|  hardening with a privileged stage or a root-level seam.\n669|- B32 The leaf-delegation wiring is measured at CUS (wrong-leaf\n670|  mutants are observable only on compliant roots); the absence\n671|  propagation through the six dispatch paths, the prober, and the\n672|  spawner is pinned by absence tests without a row. Owner: this\n673|  leaf.\n674|\n675|Carried bounds (first-leaf statements dispositioned by this leaf).\n676|B9 adapter split is discharged: the production exec, dial, probe,\n677|and spawn adapters ship (exec.go, probe.go, backend.go) and\n678|Production wires them into Dependencies; the residual is the\n679|uncomposed wiring (B27). B16 nested invocation is decided: lifecycle\n680|entries take no Ambient input, so nesting cannot collide through\n681|them (row 90); the Acquire-level over-strict nested refusal stands\n682|unchanged as first-leaf-owned. B18 sun_path is decided: strict-below\n683|per platform, counted in bytes (row 66). B19/B20 bind step is built:\n684|CheckSocketCustody enforces placement, leaf delegation, root,\n685|ancestors, and socket kind (rows 67-70). The rev7 P3-A fresh-decoy\n686|foreground attach wiring is closed: TestAcquireForegroundRefusesEveryCatalogDecoyRunning\n687|refuses every catalog-derived decoy alone and together on the\n688|foreground running path with a spawn spy silent on every member, and\n689|the attach attestation cells carry N-attach-attestation-decoy.","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
