{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000e6eb","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0c6d9-138d-7c82-92f1-7d0657d57a0f"},"sequence":4560,"recorded_at":1780531400009115,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"69dcebcf-aab8-4829-be62-f7110c555cc6","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"69dcebcf-aab8-4829-be62-f7110c555cc6","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"69dcebcf-aab8-4829-be62-f7110c555cc6"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0c70d-343b-7561-8143-bfbc46eb4fb0"},"task_id":"01a0c70d-343b-7561-8143-bfbc46eb4fb0","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0c70d-343b-7561-8143-bfbc46eb4fb0","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-84-1\",\n  \"command\": \"grep -n \\\"tmuxserver\\\\|Lifecycle\\\\|lifecycle\\\" README.md | head -n 20; echo ===; head -n 40 LOGBOOK.md 2>/dev/null || ls *.md\",\n  \"description\": \"Locate README and logbook sections\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"407:Host Credential Profile 1 lifecycle. `Open` verifies custody and converges any\\n415:the public tombstone while refusing stale or repeated lifecycle changes.\\n1702:lifecycle with compare-and-swap succession (pinned v0.5.0 Sections 2.3,\\n1703:5.1-5.2, 5.7, 14.4, plus the v0.6.0 lease lifecycle in Sections 2.2, 5.3,\\n1757:The lease lifecycle mints epoch-1 `create` leases from the durable bootstrap\\n1777:The package derives no lifecycle state, renders no list/status output, and\\n1818:lifecycle ships its own battery through\\n1898:naming its lifecycle-or-fact class and driver. `TestEventTypeUsesAreOwned`\\n1951:re-checked over the input for the same reason the lifecycle reducer\\n2215:## Terminal Instance lifecycle execution (`terminstance` engine)\\n2218:Instance lifecycle contract of the pinned Sections 4.B-4.D, 5.2, 7.A,\\n2329:## Private tmux server management (`tmuxserver` leaf)\\n2331:[`internal/tmuxserver`](internal/tmuxserver) creates owner-only runtime\\n2364:process anywhere; native Windows refuses every request. Lifecycle\\n2383:go test ./internal/tmuxserver -count=1\\n2384:go test ./internal/tmuxserver -cover -count=1\\n2391:PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 internal/tmuxserver/mutant_harness.py\\n2399:attached to `TASK-260830-35urbp`, with the lifecycle battery and its\\n2404:[the task evidence map](internal/tmuxserver/TRACEABILITY.md).\\n2545:  routes belong to the CLI/lifecycle callers that invoke revalidation.\\n===\\n# Flight Logbook\\n\\n> Institutional memory. Concise, factual, high-signal.\\n> Newest entries first. One block per insight.\\n\\n## 2026-09-22\\n\\n### TASK-260830-1c28dz — tmux lifecycle operations via structured commands (initial producer delivery)\\n\\n- SHIPPED the second `tmuxserver` leaf: `Execute` admits exactly the eight lifecycle operations (create, attach, status, quiesce, safe-boundary, stop, stale termination, restore) and refuses unknown ones; the exec adapter reconstructs the exact `tmux -S <socket> <subcommand>` vector per operation (forged binaries, flag injection, ambient discovery all refuse); the probed socket generation binds before execution (B18-B20); bodies are pure argv builders with the stable `ax pane SESSION_ID` entrypoint; effects run through the landed terminstance engine with strict per-operation deadlines, generation rechecks, and AX-side state memory, while attach/terminate/restore mirror the landed backend/fencing/axpane gates. Every mutating operation replays idempotently; uncertain receipts reconcile through status before resuming.\\n- Battery: 173 narrowing + 2 additive KILLED + control SURVIVED (100 new second-leaf narrowing rows with per-arm killers; first leaf's 76 rows still green, shared control). AC: 33 of 33 rows (59-91) driven through production entries by named tests. Second-leaf census: Table B 24×21 (10 measured), Table C 90×11 (all unreachable), Table D 90×21 (108 measured), every measured cell with a named test plus an admitting narrowing row; singleton arms bound by B22, engine-normalized status by B23.\\n- Full 30-command suite green firsthand on the frozen tree (gofmt, build, vet, full suite, race gate, cover, all fuzz gates, tracecheck, cataloggen, linux/windows builds, JSON check, board validate, diff check, windows vet); OUTCOME-keyed base-vs-candidate importer comparison clean (base 82 PASS retained, zero regressions). Evidence tarball with raw per-plant logs attached to `TASK-260830-1c28dz`. Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree.\\n- Process note: a full-suite cover gate failed while the mutant harness was still running in the same tree — the cover run compiled against a planted mutant. Re-ran clean after the harness exited 0. Never run `go test` concurrently with the harness in one worktree.\\n\\n## 2026-09-21\\n\\n### TASK-260830-35urbp rev7 — Commit-side O_DIRECTORY pin, WSL2 miss member, catalog-derived decoy completeness\\n\\n- REWORKED after review-verdict-rev6 (CHANGES REQUESTED: no P1, one P2, two P3; trunk unmoved at `799c338`, no refresh; every rev5 finding stays closed with its driven evidence kept — production behaved correctly at every point the review drove, and this revision ships no production change). The census counts reproduce mechanically (24 × 11 = 264 cells; 50 measured / 4 bounds / 210 unreachable) with per-entry kill attribution holding for all 50 measured cells.\\n- P2-A (commit-side O_DIRECTORY arm without a narrowing row): the commit side gets the verify side's fixtures — a 0700 regular-file leaf on `EnsureRuntimeDir` (admit direction) and through foreground `Acquire` (no probe, no spawn), plus a FIFO leaf on `EnsureRuntimeDir` under the shared `verifyWithDeadline` (no-hang) — and shipped row `N-containment-odirectory-commit`, named under row 5 and in the `commit × ENS` / `commit × AFG` census cells; the `N-containment-odirectory-verify` note now points at the commit row instead of asserting it. Under the plant the 0700 leaf is admitted on `Ensure` and through the entry (which probes once and spawns once into `<root>/tmux/ax.sock`) while the FIFO blocks the full 5s.\\n- P3-A (no-fallback miss arm pinned for macOS/Linux only): the Linux miss test is a platform table `{linux, wsl2}`, so `N-creation-literal` and both D rows kill through all three tmux platforms; the WSL2-guarded fallback shape now reddens on the wsl2 member only. P3-B (attestation membership pinned for one decoy of sixteen): the decoy set is derived from `catalog.Current().Capabilities` (Section 4.D, sixteen-value table asserted), every non-realm member alone and all fifteen together refuse at `CheckServerAttested` and through the background miss; `N-realm-membership` keeps its `headless_creation` member with its mask extended to the new tables. Both-spy census is 24/24 by mechanical recount.\\n- Two-sided-gate symmetry check (new instrument run against the census): every gate implemented on two or more sides compared side by side — mode 2/2, O_DIRECTORY 1/1, symlink leaf 1/1, root no-follow 1/1, session 1/1, dispatch 1/1, deps 1/1, probe 1/1, custody wiring 1/1, leaf wiring 1/1/1, details 3/3 members, absence classifier 5/5 members — all symmetric; the O_DIRECTORY commit side was the one this round closed. Optional observations taken: crash-child output captured, `TestBuildArgvRefusesInvalidArgvShape` named under B12, matrix row-46 de-duplicated, `N-details-constructor` note corrected to the typed-nil mechanism.\\n- Battery: 73 narrowing + 2 additive KILLED + control SURVIVED, 76/76 twice with identical verdicts and per-plant raw logs. AC: 58 of 58 rows driven through production entries by named tests (matrix rev7). Full 30-command suite green firsthand; `GOOS=windows GOARCH=amd64 go vet` exit 0; tmux-hidden suite 0 skip. Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree.\\n\\n### TASK-260830-35urbp rev6 — Gate × entry census instrument + broker-wiring, ownership, and session-entry pins\\n\\n- REWORKED after review-verdict-rev5 (CHANGES REQUESTED