{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000e71d","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0c6d9-138d-7c82-92f1-7d0657d57a0f"},"sequence":4585,"recorded_at":1780531400009165,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"69dcebcf-aab8-4829-be62-f7110c555cc6","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"69dcebcf-aab8-4829-be62-f7110c555cc6","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"69dcebcf-aab8-4829-be62-f7110c555cc6"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0c70d-4ca2-7c20-9e26-4b050d32f8e3"},"task_id":"01a0c70d-4ca2-7c20-9e26-4b050d32f8e3","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0c70d-4ca2-7c20-9e26-4b050d32f8e3","chunk":"Read text file `README.md`.\n(2328 line(s) above)\n2329|## Private tmux server management (`tmuxserver` leaf)\n2330|\n2331|[`internal/tmuxserver`](internal/tmuxserver) creates owner-only runtime\n2332|directories and manages dedicated `tmux -S` servers with no ambient or\n2333|default-server discovery or reuse (pinned Sections 3.2, 4.2, 4.C-4.E).\n2334|The dedicated socket is `<runtime>/tmux/ax.sock` under the Runtime IPC\n2335|root (per-user temporary directory on macOS, `$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/ax` on\n2336|Linux/WSL2), resolved by the landed `localstore` layout and supplied by\n2337|the caller; the socket is runtime IPC, never durable identity.\n2338|`EnsureRuntimeDir` commits the runtime leaf relative to a pinned root\n2339|handle (`mkdirat`, never a path-string `MkdirAll`) and enforces three\n2340|independent custody gates — containment, exact `0700` mode, effective-UID\n2341|ownership — each of which refuses alone; an existing directory is\n2342|verified, never silently repaired. `ResolveSocket` derives the one\n2343|server socket from the runtime directory and refuses any explicit\n2344|override on all five ambient members (`TMUX` and `TMUX_TMPDIR`\n2345|environment values, inherited socket, default path, conventional\n2346|`default` name). `Acquire` reaches the server through the\n2347|caller-appropriate path: foreground ensures the directory, then attaches\n2348|to the running attested server or spawns the dedicated `-S` server whose\n2349|stable pane entrypoint is `ax pane SESSION_ID`, while background\n2350|verifies the existing directory without creating it, contacts only the\n2351|already-running authenticated same-user broker and its attested server,\n2352|and a miss — including an absent runtime directory, the ordinary\n2353|post-reboot cold state — returns the typed `capability_unavailable`\n2354|refusal with realm/readiness details, while an existing-but-unsafe\n2355|directory keeps its custody refusal — there is no fallback to direct\n2356|creation, and every background-path `Acquire` test (24/24 by\n2357|mechanical census) arms both a spy spawner and a spy server probe\n2358|that fail the run if either is ever invoked. Attestation is the landed `terminalbackend`\n2359|Reconcile/ResolveEvidence admission consumed as an `Admitted` set\n2360|composed only with generation equality: a missing realm row or a\n2361|stale-generation admission refuses, so a cached observation replayed as\n2362|live authorizes nothing. Every broker, server, and spawner interaction\n2363|runs through injected dependencies, so the suite passes with no tmux\n2364|process anywhere; native Windows refuses every request. Lifecycle\n2365|operations — create, attach, status, quiesce, safe-boundary, stop,\n2366|stale termination, restore — run through structured argv builders over\n2367|the dedicated socket: `Execute` admits exactly the eight operations\n2368|and refuses unknown ones, the exec adapter reconstructs the exact\n2369|`tmux -S <socket> <subcommand>` vector per operation and refuses\n2370|forged binaries, flag injection, and ambient socket discovery, and\n2371|the probed socket generation is bound (B18-B20) before any execution.\n2372|Bodies are pure argv builders whose stable pane entrypoint stays\n2373|`ax pane SESSION_ID`; effects run through the landed terminstance\n2374|engine with strict per-operation deadlines, generation rechecks, and\n2375|AX-side state memory for reconciliation, while attach, terminate, and\n2376|restore mirror the landed backend, fencing, and axpane gates. Every\n2377|mutating operation replays the identical request idempotently;\n2378|uncertain receipts reconcile through status before resuming.\n2379|\n2380|Run the focused tests and coverage with:\n2381|\n2382|```bash\n2383|go test ./internal/tmuxserver -count=1\n2384|go test ./internal/tmuxserver -cover -count=1\n2385|```\n2386|\n2387|Run the narrowing battery (173 narrowing mutants, two supplementary\n2388|additive rows, plus one harmless control) with:\n2389|\n2390|```bash\n2391|PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 internal/tmuxserver/mutant_harness.py\n2392|```\n2393|\n2394|The harness mutates one production file in place, runs the named killer\n2395|through the production entry point, restores the file from backup, and\n2396|reports per-row verdicts with subprocess exits; `AX_MUTANT_VERBOSE=1`\n2397|additionally prints the raw per-plant logs, and `--log-dir` captures one\n2398|raw log per plant. Task validation logs and mutation artifacts are\n2399|attached to `TASK-260830-35urbp`, with the lifecycle battery and its\n2400|raw per-plant logs attached to `TASK-260830-1c28dz`. The package adds\n2401|no `ax` command, no\n2402|`doctor` result, and no runtime capability claim; the clause-to-test\n2403|matrix with its stated bounds lives in\n2404|[the task evidence map](internal/tmuxserver/TRACEABILITY.md).\n2405|\n2406|## Ownership reducer properties\n2407|\n2408|The four story-pinned ownership invariants (pinned v0.6.0 Sections 2.2, 5.3,\n(more lines below)","final_result":true}}}
