{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000edc1","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0c6d9-138d-7c82-92f1-7d0657d57a0f"},"sequence":5435,"recorded_at":1780531400010865,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"69dcebcf-aab8-4829-be62-f7110c555cc6","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"69dcebcf-aab8-4829-be62-f7110c555cc6","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"69dcebcf-aab8-4829-be62-f7110c555cc6"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0c716-6f98-7b80-bba4-89ce983d3c31"},"task_id":"01a0c716-6f98-7b80-bba4-89ce983d3c31","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0c716-6f98-7b80-bba4-89ce983d3c31","chunk":"edited\nchanged lines: lines 152-154\n--- original\n+++ updated\n@@\n-| 59 | The exec adapter runs -S vectors with AX-owned argv only: exits report as data, TMUX/TMUX_TMPDIR scrub from the child, malformed argv refuses, transport failures pass through uncoded and prove nothing. | OSRunner (exec.go) | TestOSRunnerReportsExitAsData, TestOSRunnerScrubsAmbientInChild, TestOSRunnerRefusesBadArgv, TestOSRunnerTransportErrorProvesNothing, TestScrubTmuxEnv |\n-| 60 | The primitive vocabulary is exactly the nine tmux directives and the per-operation map covers exactly the eight lifecycle operations; unknown primitives and non-lifecycle operations refuse. | ParseDirective, DirectivesFor | TestParseDirectiveAdmitsNinePrimitives, TestParseDirectiveRefusesUnknown, TestDirectivesForMapsEightOperations, TestDirectivesForRefusesNonLifecycle |\n-| 61 | Every built vector is the fixed -S shape for its directive: the socket is pinned to the runtime leaf (ambient sockets refuse), targets parse as UUIDv7, and the quiescence channel parses as UUIDv7. | BuildCommand | TestBuildCommandVectors, TestBuildCommandRefusesAmbientSocket, TestBuildCommandRefusesBadIdentity |\n+| 59 | The exec adapter runs -S vectors with AX-owned argv only: exits and both streams report as data, TMUX/TMUX_TMPDIR scrub from the child, malformed argv refuses, transport failures and signal deaths pass through as errors and prove nothing. | OSRunner (exec.go) | TestOSRunnerReportsExitAsData, TestOSRunnerCapturesStderr, TestOSRunnerSignalDeathProvesNothing, TestOSRunnerScrubsAmbientInChild, TestOSRunnerRefusesBadArgv, TestOSRunnerTransportErrorProvesNothing, TestScrubTmuxEnv |\n+| 60 | The primitive vocabulary is exactly the ten tmux directives and the per-operation map covers exactly the eight lifecycle operations; unknown primitives and non-lifecycle operations refuse. | ParseDirective, DirectivesFor | TestParseDirectiveAdmitsTenPrimitives, TestParseDirectiveRefusesUnknown, TestDirectivesForMapsEightOperations, TestDirectivesForRefusesNonLifecycle |\n+| 61 | Every built vector is the fixed -S shape for its directive: the socket is pinned to the runtime leaf (ambient sockets refuse), targets parse as UUIDv7, the quiescence channel parses as UUIDv7, the attach vector states its input authorization (read-only emits -r, unstated refuses), the boundary vector is the bare blocking wait, and detach-client addresses the session. | BuildCommand | TestBuildCommandVectors, TestBuildCommandAttachReadOnlyVector, TestBuildCommandAttachRequiresInputFlag, TestBuildCommandRefusesAmbientSocket, TestBuildCommandRefusesBadIdentity |\n","final_result":true}}}
