{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000fed7","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0c6d9-138d-7c82-92f1-7d0657d57a0f"},"sequence":7622,"recorded_at":1780531400015239,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"69dcebcf-aab8-4829-be62-f7110c555cc6","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"69dcebcf-aab8-4829-be62-f7110c555cc6","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"69dcebcf-aab8-4829-be62-f7110c555cc6"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0c748-0629-77b3-a34a-2a30ad77d22e"},"task_id":"01a0c748-0629-77b3-a34a-2a30ad77d22e","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0c748-0629-77b3-a34a-2a30ad77d22e","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-176-1\",\n  \"command\": \"tail -n 30 LOGBOOK.md; echo =====; head -n 50 /tmp/c28dz/results-draft.md; echo =====; wc -l /tmp/c28dz/results-draft.md /tmp/c28dz/matrix.md /tmp/c28dz/matrix-new.md\",\n  \"description\": \"Review logbook and drafts\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"\\n## 2026-09-10 (later)\\n\\n### TASK-260909-2ez769 rework — CR3 changes-requested repaired on base a89328c\\n- SCOPE: same candidate, no base move (adoption trunk already in). All five CR3 findings addressed in `internal/hosttrust` + `internal/config`; no RPC absorption (4 tracked RPC paths verified CLEAN, parked 11/11 intact, no rpcwire remnants).\\n- P1 STALE MUTATION: `WithMutationAuthorization` no longer refreshes the cached generation; a binding older than committed refuses `ErrStaleGeneration` (`authorize.go`). Committed `TestWithMutationAuthorizationRefusesStaleGeneration` + narrowing plant `stale-mutation-refresh` (KILLED).\\n- P1 BOUNDARY/REVOKE: lock descriptors are per-acquisition (unix `flock`, Windows `LockFileEx`), so same-process goroutines serialize like separate processes; lock-file creation guarded by a process mutex; `Initialize` no longer re-acquires (unlocked nested read + documented no-reentry discipline). Existing serialization test hardened to the deterministic 250ms contention shape. Narrowing coverage via `revoke-state` + serialization tests.\\n- P1 CRASH ATOMICITY: new joint commit (`joint.go`): closed `PendingCommit` marker, `JointCommit` (in-lock revalidation + marker + replace + bump + unmark), `Recover` (forward/abort/refuse) auto-run by `Open`. `CommitConfigChange` removed (it encoded the split-brain pattern). Apply/rollback revalidate preview/source/generation/custody inside the exclusive hold; post-bump failures restore source + converge via `Recover` (`ErrJointReplacementDurable`). Committed real child-process crash test (`TestApplyV4CrashConvergesGeneration`, exit 77) plus abort/intervention/already-bumped/exhaustion unit tests. Power-loss vs process-crash documented honestly (fsync-durable, disk-dependent).\\n- P1 WINDOWS DACL: `verifyOwner` now audits owner SID plus every DACL allow entry (null/empty/deny-only/unknown-type fail closed); creation paths install protected owner-only DACLs (`secureStaged`); Unix mode checks abstracted via `platformModeOK` (exact 0700/0600 preserved). Pure `ownerOnlyGrants` evaluator tested on darwin (9 cases). No Windows runner exists here: evidence is GOOS=windows build + vet clean, unit tests, and an explicit stated bound (no invented runtime pass).\\n- P2 EXCLUSION: `ExcludedFromReplication` gains the joint marker; new `MatchExcludedFromReplication` (staging prefixes, fail-closed escapes) and `ExcludedConfigDirName` (.bak./.pre-rollback./.ax-config-*) with custody-walk + published-backup-name tests. No in-repo replication/snapshot/export-of-state surface exists (sessadapter/localstore/dirnode do not touch host-channel); outcome hands consumers + required tests to future export surfaces. Config claim corrected: 4 semantic narrowing + 1 label-precision kill (label plant marked LABEL-PRECISION in-table).\\n- ROW 13: new production `LoadCoherent` (config+trust under one shared hold) + serialization test.\\n- VALIDATION (rerun this run, exit 0): gofmt clean; `go vet ./...`; `go test ./... -count=1` all ok (281 top-level PASS across hosttrust/config/peeridentity/secprim); `-cover` hosttrust 77.8 config 93.1 peeridentity 97.5 secprim 94.4; `-race` on hosttrust+config ok; tracecheck ok; catalog v0.6.0 -check ok; linux+windows amd64 builds ok; `git diff --check` clean; refusal-inventory audit green (new sites covered by direct revalidation/helper tests); census green. Mutation batteries rerun exact-source: hosttrust 18 narrowing KILLED + neutral passed; config 4 semantic + 1 label KILLED + neutral passed (manifests bound to a89328c in mutations-*-rework/).\\n- STATUS: ready for review, worktree UNCOMMITTED for handoff snapshot. `task-board validate` shows 231 pre-existing board-wide ledger-mirror issues, none referencing this task.\\n\\n### TASK-260909-2ez769 rework rev8 — CR7 resource binding and typed write-path census\\n- BASE: managed `task-board worktree refresh-candidate TASK-260909-2ez769` advanced the candidate to protected AX trunk `8626fb361c1d6b62d5f95c7be4cb33c85d4aadf3`, replaying the checkpointed SSH/peer leaves. The RPC backup manifest and parked RPC delta remain preserved; no RPC implementation path was absorbed. Candidate branch head is `305875134f8d344eb86ef926c7fbca3fed85c49d` and remains uncommitted.\\n- FIX (F2): `HeldExclusive` now carries the exact trust-store root/lock identity and an explicit configuration-path binding. `requireHoldForRoot` protects hosttrust mutations; `ValidateConfigPath` protects Config4/legacy pair writes; `JointCommit` binds the marker path before replace/restore callbacks; legacy migration uses `WithExclusiveHoldForConfig`. A genuine hold from a different Store refuses before staging while the target lock is live (`TestWriteTempReplaceRefusesForeignStoreHold`). Zero, released, same-store, and unbound live holds are all production-position negative tests.\\n- FIX (F1): the Config/Host Trust Store write-path gate now loads production packages with `golang.org/x/tools/go/packages` and resolves `go/types` objects by package path, receiver, and method identity. It covers direct OS mutations, backend/interface methods, aliases, function/method values, map/struct fields, package initializers/IIFEs, closures, interface implementations, generic helpers, and unresolved callees (fail closed). The five CR7 plants plus direct controls and new interface/generic shapes have executable behavioral witnesses.\\n- EVIDENCE: `go test ./... -count=1` exit 0 (`.temp/TASK-260909-2ez769/go-test-all-01.log`); `go test ./... -cover` exit 0 (`config 93.5%`, `hosttrust 77.5%`, `.temp/TASK-260909-2ez769/go-test-cover-01.log`); `go vet ./...`, native build, GOOS=windows build/vet, gofmt, and `git diff --check` all exit 0. Census run: `writepath-census-02.log`. Narrowing mutants: `hold-resource-skip` killed by `TestHeldExclusiveRejectsUnboundConfigPath`; `replace-require-skip` killed by zero-hold production tests; token-preserving `writepath-method-value-skip` killed by `TestWritePathGateFlagsExecutableRogues/backend_method_value`. Raw mutation JSON/table are under `.temp/TASK-260909-2ez769/mutations-{hold-resource,config-hold,writepath}-*/`.\\n- COVERAGE RATIO: 19 of 21 previously enumerated production acceptance rows are driven by named entry-point tests; 2 remain stated bounds (Windows runtime DACL execution and a future export/replication consumer surface absent from this repository). No claim is made for those bounds.\\n- STATUS: ready for review; worktree intentionally UNCOMMITTED for Story handoff snapshot.\\n\\n### TASK-260909-2ez769 rework rev9 — CR8 narrowing closures for typed write census and Store-owned Config binding\\n- BASE: unchanged from rev8: candidate checkpoint `305875134f8d344eb86ef926c7fbca3fed85c49d`, protected AX trunk `8626fb361c1d6b62d5f95c7be4cb33c85d4aadf3`. The 15-file RPC backup manifest, parked RPC delta, and checkpointed SSH/peer work remain preserved; no RPC implementation path was absorbed.\\n- FIX (F1): the production-source write-path census now resolves `go/types` function identities for bare identifiers and selectors, while rejecting writer-shaped indirect callees unless they are an exact censused definition in the current Go build context. The census rejects dot-imported function values, promoted embedded backend methods, package-level slice writer functions, function-typed struct fields and parameters, and dot-imported composite-literal function values. `isHoldEntryCall` uses exact package/receiver/method identity, so a same-named impostor method is not an entry gate.\\n- FIX (F2): `WithExclusiveHoldForConfig` is Store-owned. A generic or foreign Store cannot bind an arbitrary existing Config path; a configured Store can bind only its canonical paired path. Refusal occurs before staging/bytes mutation. The narrowing mutant drops the unconfigured-store refusal while retaining the other path checks and is killed by `TestWithExclusiveHoldForConfigRefusesUnconfiguredStorePath`.\\n- EVIDENCE: `writepath-method-value-skip` preserves the searched token while weakening the typed method-value gate and is killed by `TestWritePathGateFlagsExecutableRogues/backend_method_value`; controls have executable witnesses for all six CR8 shapes. Hosttrust `hold-resource-skip` is killed by the unconfigured foreign-resource test. Final artifacts are under `.temp/TASK-260909-2ez769/mutations-{config,hosttrust}-rev9/`.\\n- COVERAGE RATIO: 19 of 21 enumerated production acceptance rows are driven by named production-entry tests. The two stated bounds remain: Windows runtime DACL execution is not available on this Darwin runner, and this repository has no export/replication consumer surface for host-trust secret exclusion. No claim is made for either bound.\\n- VALIDATION: grouped full suite `go test -count=1 -v` A/B/C/D all exit 0 across all 26 packages; grouped full coverage A/B/C/D all exit 0 (`config 93.5%`, `hosttrust 77.9%`, `peeridentity 97.5%`); scoped hosttrust/config/peeridentity tests, scoped vet, native/Linux-arm64/Windows-amd64 builds, Windows test compilation, `go mod tidy -diff`, and `git diff --check` are green. Logs and package inventory are in `.temp/TASK-260909-2ez769/`.\\n- STATUS: ready for review; worktree remains intentionally UNCOMMITTED for Story handoff snapshot.\\n=====\\n# TASK-260830-1c28dz rework rev2 — results (DRAFT: race + final harness pending)\\n\\n## Verdict\\n\\nAll six rev1 blocking findings (P1-A…P1-E, P2-A, P2-B) are closed with\\ndriven evidence. AC rows 59–91: 33 of 33 driven through production\\nentries by named committed tests. Operations: 8 of 8 through `Execute`.\\n\\n## Finding closures\\n\\n### P1-A safe-boundary barrier/boundary protocol — CLOSED\\n\\n- Boundary vector is the bare blocking `wait-for <channel>` (verified\\n  against tmux 3.6a `list-commands` + manual: bare form blocks until\\n  `wait-for -S`; `-L` acquires a lock and succeeds immediately).\\n  Killer: `TestExecuteBoundaryWaitsForSignal` (exact argv, no -L/-S/-U)\\n  + `N-boundary-blocking-vector`.\\n- Proof kind carried: `executeEngineOp` sets `backend.proofKind` from\\n  `Params`; `observeBoundary` binds it into evidence; provider kinds\\n  bind contemporaneous `list-panes` rows as best-effort context\\n  (never failing the signaled proof). Killers:\\n  `TestExecuteBoundaryBindsProofKind` (quiescence vs process-exit,\\n  same rows/time → different evidence) + `N-boundary-proof-kind`;\\n  `TestObserveBoundaryBindsProviderRows`.\\n- Barrier: quiesce runs `lock-session` then `detach-client -s`\\n  (verified: `lock-session` locks only currently attached clients —\\n  a newly attaching client gets an unlocked shell — and `detach-client\\n  -s` detaches all current clients of the session); new\\n  input-authorized attaches refuse at `executeAttach` once quiescing\\n  records (`local_precondition_failed` / `attach quiesced input`);\\n  read-only attaches stay admitted (observation retained); quiesce\\n  emits no `send-keys` (only the ordered request-stop effect sends).\\n  Killers: `TestExecuteQuiesceBarrierSequence`,\\n  `TestExecuteAttachRefusesInputWhenQuiescing`,\\n  `TestExecuteQuiesceEmitsNoProviderInput`,\\n  `TestExecuteQuiesceRefusesFailedClose` + rows `N-quiesce-detach-step`,\\n  `N-quiesce-attach-gate`, `N-quiesce-sendkeys-absent`,\\n  `N-quiesce-close-exit`, `N-cmdvector-detach`.\\n- Stated bound B33: the wrapper `wait-for -S` signal step is\\n  unimplemented in the landed wrapper, so boundary waits time out\\n  fail-closed (`quiesce_timeout`) until it lands. Owner: wrapper task.\\n\\n### P1-B read-only attach vector — CLOSED\\n\\n- `BuildCommand` takes the input authorization and emits\\n  `attach-session -r` for `input_authorized=false` (man: read-only\\n  clients only detach/switch), writable otherwise; unstated\\n  authorization refuses (`tmux_invalid_arguments` /\\n  `command attach authorization`). Killers:\\n  `TestExecuteReadOnlyAttachIsReadOnly` (entry, both directions),\\n=====\\n     173 /tmp/c28dz/results-draft.md\\n     444 /tmp/c28dz/matrix.md\\n     515 /tmp/c28dz/matrix-new.md\\n    1132 total\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 11906,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 2977,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
