 `TestExecuteTerminateUnknownConfirmIsNotTerminated` + rows\n72|  `N-probe-negative-exit`, `N-probe-unmarked-exit`.\n73|- Stated bound B35: markers verified on tmux 3.6a; other versions\n74|  fail closed to unknown.\n75|\n76|### P1-D custody symlink traversal — CLOSED\n77|\n78|- `checkCustodyAncestors` walks the lexical path with per-prefix\n79|  `secprim.OpenNoFollowDir` (no `EvalSymlinks`); `checkCustodyRoot`\n80|  opens no-follow, verifies through the descriptor, and binds the\n81|  handle back to the path (`os.SameFile`, seam-tested). Details\n82|  preserved (`socket root`, `socket ancestor`). Killers:\n83|  `TestCheckSocketCustodyRefusesIntermediateSymlink`,\n84|  `TestSocketCustodySymlinkRefusesAtProbeAndSpawn` (before-connect +\n85|  before-bind), `TestCheckSocketCustodyNoCacheAfterChange`,\n86|  `TestCheckSocketCustodyIdentityMismatchRefuses` + rows\n87|  `N-custody-alias-skip`, `N-custody-identity-bind`.\n88|\n89|### P1-E restore binding + after-restore sequence — CLOSED\n90|\n91|- Create keeps the carried binding document beside the bootstrap\n92|  receipt (`InstanceStates.RecordBindingDoc`); restore re-admits it\n93|  through `termbind.ParseTerminalBinding`, checks session/instance/\n94|  backend/generation agreement, and returns it (nothing minted).\n95|  Killers: `TestExecuteRestoreReturnsBinding`,\n96|  `TestExecuteRestoreRefusesSwappedBindingDoc`,\n97|  `TestExecuteCreatePersistsBindingDocForRestore` (create→reboot→\n98|  restore end to end), `TestExecuteCreateRefusesBindingDocFailure` +\n99|  rows `N-restore-binding-omit`, `N-restore-agreement-session`,\n100|  `N-create-doc-persist`, `N-binddoc-session-identity`,\n101|  `N-binddoc-lookup-identity`, `N-binddoc-document-shape`.\n102|- After-restore branch in `executeRestore`: local lease read →\n103|  bounded mesh refresh (default 5000 ms, measured) → resume iff\n104|  local holds the winning tuple + material valid; remote offer iff\n105|  another host holds + interactive; else parked, never launching.\n106|  Killers: `TestExecuteRestoreRemoteOfferOnLapsedGrant`,\n107|  `TestExecuteRestoreOffersWhenRemoteHoldsLocalTuple`,\n108|  `TestExecuteRestoreResumesUnderLocalLease`,\n109|  `TestExecuteRestoreParksOtherwise` (5 subtests),\n110|  `TestExecuteRestoreRefreshBounded` (deadline + blocking-refresh)\n111|  + rows `N-restore-branch-offer/holder/tuple/material/remote`,\n112|  `N-refresh-bound-default`.\n113|\n114|### P2-A replay timestamps — CLOSED\n115|\n116|- `InstanceStates.RecordOutcome/LookupOutcome` persist the\n117|  quiesce/boundary report per idempotency key; first success\n118|  records, retries replay. Killers:\n119|  `TestExecuteQuiesceReplayKeepsTimestamps`,\n120|  `TestExecuteBoundaryReplayKeepsProofAndTime` (clock-advanced),\n121|  `TestOutcomeRecordCrashConverges` (hook-failed first record →\n122|  retry records, third stable, evidence unchanged, no second\n123|  effect), `TestInstanceStatesOutcomeRoundTrip` + rows\n124|  `N-replay-timestamp-quiesce/boundary`, `N-outcome-key-record`.\n125|- Stated bound B34: a crash between receipt commit and outcome\n126|  record re-observes the report time (no second effect, same proof).\n127|\n128|### P2-B census + comparison — CLOSED\n129|\n130|- rootwrite/ancestorwrite × status/restore reclassified U2a → M:\n131|  `TestExecuteCustodyEntryRoots` (4 subtests, literal messages) +\n132|  4 `N-custody-entry-*` rows (reviewer's exact shapes, committed).\n133|- Symmetry paragraph carries per-side admitting-row counts for\n134|  every multi-side/multi-member gate (shared rows noted).\n135|- Ratio restated from a mechanical recount: 208 measured of 4448\n136|  (50+10+148), 34 bound, 4206 unreachable.\n137|- Fixed witness names: `TestExecuteRefusesMissingDependencies`\n138|  (was `...NilDependencies`), plus the created\n139|  `TestExecuteRestoreIdempotent`,\n140|  `TestExecuteStatusPresentIncludesIdentity`,\n141|  `TestObserveStatusAbsentProbe`.\n142|- OUTCOME-keyed comparison over the complete 34-package importer\n143|  closure (JSON event grids, top-level + subtests): 2662 shared\n144|  top-level inputs and 20345 shared subtests, ZERO moved; 205\n145|  top-level + 169 subtest additions, all PASS, all in tmuxserver;\n146|  zero removed. No input moved across any admission/refusal arm.\n147|\n148|## Census and battery (PENDING final harness rerun)\n149|\n150|- Table D: 115 × 21 = 2415 cells; 148 M, 30 B, 2237 U (script).\n151|- Battery: 207 narrowing rows (134 second-leaf) + 2 additive + control.\n152|\n153|## Validation (PENDING race + final harness)\n154|\n155|- Fast gates 1-3, 24-30: PASS (incl. tracecheck, cataloggen, linux/\n156|  windows builds, windows vet exit 0, board validate exit 0).\n157|- Full suite (cmd 4): exit 0, 3083 top-level PASS, 0 FAIL.\n158|- Cover (cmd 6): exit 0. Fuzz 7-23: all PASS.\n159|- tmuxserver coverage: 87.4%.\n160|- Race (cmd 5): PENDING.\n161|- No-tmux proof: PENDING.\n162|- Final full harness: PENDING.\n163|\n164|## Reviewer rev1 file, verbatim rerun\n165|\n166|6 of 7 pass unmodified against this candidate\n167|(`TestReviewStopUnknownExit`, `TestReviewCustodyIntermediateSymlink`,\n168|`TestReviewBoundaryNeedsSignal`, `TestReviewReadOnlyAttach`,\n169|`TestReviewCustodyEntryRoots` 4/4, `TestReviewRestoreRequiredBinding`).\n170|`TestReviewQuiesceReplayTimestamp` needs its one-line script update\n171|(the P1-A barrier runs `detach-client` after `lock-session`, which\n172|rev1 demanded): the committed `TestExecuteQuiesceReplayKeepsTimestamps`\n173|is the adapted witness and passes.","final_result":true}}}
