 2; deadline EXA 1 / EXT 1 / EXR 2; keymaterial EXT 1 / EXR\n356|1; capdual EXT 2 members; fencingmap EXT 2 + 3 pinned; target EXT 3\n357|members; winner EXT 2 members (session arm U3: fencing+target\n358|precede); record EXT 1 / EXR 1 shared + UNT 1; replay EXT 2 + 6\n359|pinned; bindmap/bindfound single-sided at EXT; readonly EXA 1 / CMD 1\n360|shared; detachvec CMD 1; boundarykind/boundexit EXE 1 each + PFX\n361|0/1; quiescedetach EXE 1 / PFX 1 shared; nosendkeys/closeexit EXE 1\n362|each; probemarker EXS 1 / EXE 1 / EXT 1 shared; probeneg EXE 1;\n363|identity CUS 1; bindcontract/restoreagree EXR 1 each; replaytime EXE\n364|2; afterRestoreBranch holder/tuple/material/remote/offer/bound 1\n365|each (all EXR); refreshbound EXR 1; outcomekey REC 1 / LOOK 0 (B22\n366|singleton); binddocid REC 1 / LOOK 1; binddocshape REC 1; docpersist\n367|EXR 1; Table B verify 9 new-entry sides shared 1, server EXA 1 (its\n368|other sides are first-leaf symmetry).\n369|\n370|Ratio: 208 measured of 4448 (50+10+148 M across Tables A/B/D;\n371|Table C all U); 34 bound; 4206 unreachable with reasons. Every\n372|driven refusal direction is measured except the bound cells: 22\n373|driven but rowless (B22 singletons/forks, B23 normalized details,\n374|B29 poll past-deadline, B32 propagation) and 8 named undriven gaps\n375|(B24/B25/B26/B28/B31 cells, B29 dispatch side), each with its owner\n376|below.\n377|\n378|## Bounds (mirrored B22-B35 plus carried dispositions)\n379|\n380|- B22 Singleton arms ship no narrowing mutant: admitting the\n381|  singleton refused member is deleting the gate. Covered sites, each\n382|  test-pinned in both directions where a fork exists: create relay\n383|  transport (relay), descriptor presence fork (descpresence),\n384|  attach admission nil (serveadmitnil), spawner runner nil\n385|  (spawnnil), reconcile verifier nil (reconcilenil), states root\n386|  empty (stateopen), persist/attach stores nil (storenil),\n387|  failed-kill self-confirm (selfconfirm), live-after-escalation\n388|  (stoptimeout), outcome-lookup empty key (outcomekey LOOK side;\n389|  the record side narrows over its operation member). Owner: this\n390|  leaf; retest if any site grows a second refused member.\n391|- B23 The landed status engine normalizes backend error details to\n392|  \"status observation unknown\" (coded or not), so the cutrow and\n393|  empty-panes narrowings measure at the helper entries while the\n394|  dispatch legs pin the code. Owner: this leaf; retest if the\n395|  engine stops normalizing.\n396|- B24 The idempotency-store Completed read-failure arm is unstaged:\n397|  no seam fails receipt reads (hooks fire on write paths only).\n398|  Owner: hardening; stage with a read-failure seam to measure.\n399|- B25 The Bind clean-miss sub-arm is unstageable: every Bind error\n400|  the hooks stage leaves the committed file, so Lookup always finds\n401|  it. The clean-found sub-arm is measured (N-bind-hook-found).\n402|  Owner: hardening.\n403|- B26 The attach effect-failure dispatch mapping is unstaged: no\n404|  committed failure reaches it (the store replays identical\n405|  receipts; conflicting receipts are untested at dispatch).\n406|  Owner: hardening.\n407|- B27 No committed test composes the Production Dependencies into\n408|  Acquire: AFG reaches the adapter and bind gates only through\n409|  caller-injected implementations (the 19 Table C U2c cells). The\n410|  injection seam is first-leaf-owned; Production wiring is\n411|  unit-pinned (TestProductionWiresDependencies). Owner: composition\n412|  test, sibling scope.\n413|- B28 The backend command-error wrap is unmeasured at PFX (no\n414|  backend test stages a refused build; the builder rows pin the\n415|  refused shapes at CMD). Owner: this leaf; retest with a\n416|  refused-build backend test.\n417|- B29 The close-confirm poll deadline is pinned for past-deadline\n418|  at PFX via direct staging; the exact-boundary member and\n419|  dispatch-level staging are unmeasured (the fake runner advances\n420|  no time). Owner: hardening.\n421|- B30 The OSRunner exit/transport/argv mappings are total functions\n422|  over uncoded inputs with no refused class to admit a member of;\n423|  tests pin them including real-exec scrub, stderr-capture, and\n424|  signal-death integrations. The signal-death arm (a killed child\n425|  errors instead of reporting -1 data) is a refused class and\n426|  carries its own narrowing row; the remaining mappings stay total.\n427|  Owner: this leaf.\n428|- B31 The custody root-ownership arm is untested and singleton: the\n429|  ownership seam stages leaf-first (the leaf refuses before the\n430|  root arm runs), and a truly foreign root needs privilege. Owner:\n431|  hardening with a privileged stage or a root-level seam.\n432|- B32 The leaf-delegation wiring is measured at CUS (wrong-leaf\n433|  mutants are observable only on compliant roots); the absence\n434|  propagation through the six dispatch paths, the prober, and the\n435|  spawner is pinned by absence tests without a row. Owner: this\n436|  leaf.\n437|- B33 The wrapper safe-boundary signal step is unimplemented in the\n438|  landed wrapper: the boundary entry waits blocking on\n439|  `ax-boundary-<generation>` for the wrapper's `wait-for -S`, and\n440|  the wrapper never signals today, so boundary waits time out with\n441|  the coded quiesce_timeout (fail closed, never a faked proof)\n442|  until the signal step lands. The wait vector, the proof-kind\n443|  binding, the provider-row context, and the timeout are this\n444|  leaf's and fully driven; the signal emission is the wrapper's.\n445|  Owner: the wrapper (`ax pane`) task; retest the full\n446|  quiesce-boundary-stop flow when the signal lands.\n447|- B34 A crash between the mutation-receipt commit and the operation\n448|  outcome record re-observes the report time on retry: the effect\n449|  never re-runs and the evidence never changes, but the reported\n450|  closure/boundary time renders from the retry clock instead of\n451|  the original one. Sequential retries without a crash replay\n452|  identical times. Owner: this leaf; closing the window needs the\n453|  outcome inside the engine-owned receipt.\n454|- B35 The absence stderr markers are verified against tmux 3.6a\n455|  (`can't find session`, `can't find window`, and the\n456|  no-such-socket connect error); any other version's\n457|  absence-shaped stderr fails closed to unknown. Owner: this leaf;\n458|  re-verify the marker set when the tmux floor version moves.\n459|\n460|Carried bounds (first-leaf statements dispositioned by this leaf).\n461|B9 adapter split is discharged: the production exec, dial, probe,\n462|and spawn adapters ship (exec.go, probe.go, backend.go) and\n463|Production wires them into Dependencies; the residual is the\n464|uncomposed wiring (B27). B16 nested invocation is decided: lifecycle\n465|entries take no Ambient input, so nesting cannot collide through\n466|them (row 90); the Acquire-level over-strict nested refusal stands\n467|unchanged as first-leaf-owned. B18 sun_path is decided: strict-below\n468|per platform, counted in bytes (row 66). B19/B20 bind step is built:\n469|CheckSocketCustody enforces placement, leaf delegation, root,\n470|ancestors, and socket kind (rows 67-70); the bind step refuses\n471|intermediate symlinks through no-follow opens, which is stricter\n472|than the B11 Acquire rule it stands beside. The rev7 P3-A fresh-decoy\n473|foreground attach wiring is closed: TestAcquireForegroundRefusesEveryCatalogDecoyRunning\n474|refuses every catalog-derived decoy alone and together on the\n475|foreground running path with a spawn spy silent on every member, and\n476|the attach attestation cells carry N-attach-attestation-decoy. New\n477|bounds this revision: B33 states the unimplemented wrapper boundary\n478|signal (fail-closed timeout until it lands), B34 the receipt/outcome\n479|crash window, and B35 the tmux-version marker set.\n480|\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
