pass with logs attached\\\"}},{\\\"ok\\\":true,\\\"result\\\":{\\\"checked\\\":true,\\\"id\\\":\\\"TASK-260830-1c28dz\\\",\\\"item\\\":3,\\\"text\\\":\\\"README/doctor/capability evidence and specification traceability are updated without unsupported claims\\\"}},{\\\"ok\\\":true,\\\"result\\\":{\\\"checked\\\":true,\\\"id\\\":\\\"TASK-260830-1c28dz\\\",\\\"item\\\":4,\\\"text\\\":\\\"A gate x entry census is committed as a table in the conformance matrix and mirrored in TRACEABILITY: every production entry that reaches each gate gets a named test plus an admitting narrowing row, or unreachable with a reason, or a stated bound with an owner; every gate implemented on two or more sides carries a row-count symmetry line\\\"}},{\\\"ok\\\":true,\\\"result\\\":{\\\"checked\\\":true,\\\"id\\\":\\\"TASK-260830-1c28dz\\\",\\\"item\\\":7,\\\"text\\\":\\\"The bounds 35urbp handed over are each dispositioned: B18 sun_path 104-byte limit on the derived socket path, B16 nested invocation from inside an AX pane (ambient collision, decide deliberately), B19/B20 SPEC 810-812 before-bind rejection of an unsafe root at the bind step, and the rev7 P3-A fresh-decoy foreground attach wiring if attach semantics land here rather than in g0pcnt\\\"}},{\\\"ok\\\":true,\\\"result\\\":{\\\"checked\\\":true,\\\"id\\\":\\\"TASK-260830-1c28dz\\\",\\\"item\\\":8,\\\"text\\\":\\\"Composing packages keep working, proven by an OUTCOME-keyed comparison over the complete importer set (not a name-keyed per-test diff of one package), with every input that moved across an admission or refusal arm named in the results\\\"}},{\\\"ok\\\":true,\\\"result\\\":{\\\"checked\\\":true,\\\"id\\\":\\\"TASK-260830-1c28dz\\\",\\\"item\\\":9,\\\"text\\\":\\\"Every rule is driven to its effect by a committed test that passes with NO tmux process anywhere; any real-tmux test is separately gated and is never the only witness for an acceptance row, and the results state which rows have a real-tmux witness in addition to their deterministic one\\\"}},{\\\"ok\\\":true,\\\"result\\\":{\\\"checked\\\":true,\\\"id\\\":\\\"TASK-260830-1c28dz\\\",\\\"item\\\":10,\\\"text\\\":\\\"Code written per task description and AC\\\"}},{\\\"ok\\\":true,\\\"result\\\":{\\\"checked\\\":true,\\\"id\\\":\\\"TASK-260830-1c28dz\\\",\\\"item\\\":13,\\\"text\\\":\\\"Every command, message, state, or refusal named in the AC is driven through the production entry point by a named committed test, or is declared a stated bound. Report coverage as a ratio — `n of m AC rows driven` — and name the production call site for each. Prose in place of the ratio is not evidence.\\\"}},{\\\"ok\\\":true,\\\"result\\\":{\\\"checked\\\":true,\\\"id\\\":\\\"TASK-260830-1c28dz\\\",\\\"item\\\":14,\\\"text\\\":\\\"Gating, refusing, validating, authorizing, or attesting behavior covered by negative tests that fail when the gate admits what it must reject, with the production call site named\\\"}},{\\\"ok\\\":true,\\\"result\\\":{\\\"checked\\\":true,\\\"id\\\":\\\"TASK-260830-1c28dz\\\",\\\"item\\\":15,\\\"text\\\":\\\"Every gate ships at least one NARROWING mutant — the gate stays present and is weakened to admit exactly one member of the class it must reject, and a named test must fail. A delete-only mutant proves only that the gate exists and is not accepted as evidence.\\\"}},{\\\"ok\\\":true,\\\"result\\\":{\\\"checked\\\":true,\\\"id\\\":\\\"TASK-260830-1c28dz\\\",\\\"item\\\":21,\\\"text\\\":\\\"Implementation matches AC\\\"}},{\\\"ok\\\":true,\\\"result\\\":{\\\"checked\\\":true,\\\"id\\\":\\\"TASK-260830-1c28dz\\\",\\\"item\\\":22,\\\"text\\\":\\\"Solution fits project architecture\\\"}},{\\\"ok\\\":true,\\\"result\\\":{\\\"checked\\\":true,\\\"id\\\":\\\"TASK-260830-1c28dz\\\",\\\"item\\\":23,\\\"text\\\":\\\"Tests green\\\"}}]\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 3634,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 909,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
